  "description": "Erection of outbuilding to rear garden and the erection of a front porch",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed front porch, by reason of its siting, scale, height and design, would form a visually prominent and overly dominant addition on the principal elevation of the host dwelling. The development would fail to appear subordinate and would not integrate with the architectural composition of the existing property, resulting in an incongruous and harmful feature within the street scene. As such, the proposal would detract from the character and appearance of the host dwelling and the surrounding area, contrary to Policies BE1 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part One Strategic Policies (2012) and Policies DMHB11 and DMHD1 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part Two - Development Management Policies (2020).",
    "The proposed development would result in the removal of an existing tree and associated landscaping; however, insufficient information has been submitted to assess the quality, condition and amenity value of the affected vegetation. In particular, no tree survey or supporting arboricultural information has been provided. As such, it has not been demonstrated that the loss of this landscaping would not result in harm to the character and appearance of the site and the wider area, nor has any appropriate mitigation or replacement planting been secured. The proposal therefore fails to comply with Policy DMHB14 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part Two - Development Management Policies (2020), which seeks to safeguard existing trees and ensure suitable replacement where loss is proposed."
  ],
